WEBVTT

00:01.582 --> 00:03.184
PIKACHU:
 Pika!

00:04.552 --> 00:09.657
( trumpets playing )

00:09.690 --> 00:11.325
ANNOUNCER:
 The Poké Ball,

00:11.358 --> 00:13.561
 an invention that's captured
the imagination

00:13.594 --> 00:14.796
 of people everywhere.

00:14.829 --> 00:16.431
 Thanks to its ability

00:16.464 --> 00:19.100
 to capture the most marvelous
of creatures,

00:19.133 --> 00:20.501
 Pokémon.

00:20.534 --> 00:21.602
 And to catch one

00:21.635 --> 00:23.471
 is an experience
like none other.

00:23.504 --> 00:25.506
 Each of these
spectacular species

00:25.539 --> 00:27.542
 has amazing powers
and attributes

00:27.575 --> 00:29.410
 that set them apart
from one another

00:29.443 --> 00:32.180
 in ways too numerous to list.

00:32.213 --> 00:34.182
 But unique as they are
individually,

00:34.215 --> 00:35.450
 together they make up

00:35.483 --> 00:38.453
 the incredible world
of Pokémon.

01:08.716 --> 01:10.351
( growling )

01:12.753 --> 01:16.224
Golem. Golem.

01:17.925 --> 01:19.460
Geodude.
Geodude.

01:19.493 --> 01:21.262
Geo. Geodude.

01:21.295 --> 01:23.631
Haunter. Haunter. Haunter.

01:25.499 --> 01:29.504
( growls )

01:33.440 --> 01:35.243
Primeape.

01:44.785 --> 01:49.357
Wingull.

01:56.197 --> 01:58.199
Tentacool.

01:58.232 --> 02:00.168
Magikarp. Magikarp.

02:00.201 --> 02:01.936
Sharpedo!

02:01.969 --> 02:04.472
 Pokémon and people
like Ash Ketchum

02:04.505 --> 02:06.474
 can come together as a team.

02:06.507 --> 02:08.543
 For once they're captured
in a Poké Ball,

02:08.576 --> 02:10.845
 Pokémon bond with their human
trainers

02:10.878 --> 02:13.514
 as friends, partners, family.

02:13.547 --> 02:15.850
 On their journey of discovery,

02:15.883 --> 02:17.385
 trainers and their Pokémon

02:17.418 --> 02:20.655
 learn as much about themselves
as each other.

02:20.688 --> 02:22.223
 And they also realize

02:22.256 --> 02:23.624
 that there will always be
more Pokémon

02:23.657 --> 02:25.493
 than they could have
ever imagined.

02:25.526 --> 02:27.795
 You see, for each Pokémon
that's discovered,

02:27.828 --> 02:29.830
 there are dozens,
perhaps hundreds more

02:29.863 --> 02:31.699
 we have yet to meet.

02:31.732 --> 02:33.367
 One thing's for sure,

02:33.400 --> 02:36.437
 with each of these new Pokémon
come new possibilities,

02:36.470 --> 02:40.542
 new stories, new friendships,
and new adventures.

02:43.377 --> 02:46.781
( upbeat theme playing )

03:01.662 --> 03:02.763
Venusaur.

03:02.797 --> 03:05.967
 Perhaps Pokémon trainers
aren't the only ones

03:06.000 --> 03:07.902
 to seek out new species.

03:07.935 --> 03:10.938
 The Pokémon themselves seem
to have an innate curiosity

03:10.971 --> 03:14.542
 for the creatures of this world
and of worlds beyond.

03:14.575 --> 03:15.676
 After all,

03:15.709 --> 03:17.778
 we may live
on a Pokémon planet,

03:17.811 --> 03:21.249
 but nobody ever said
that it's the only one.

03:23.017 --> 03:25.353
( dramatic theme playing )

03:39.900 --> 03:41.769
( majestic theme playing )

04:12.366 --> 04:15.737
( mellow theme playing )

04:35.122 --> 04:37.458
( indistinct chattering )

04:48.635 --> 04:51.939
Professor,
have you seen Tory?

04:51.972 --> 04:53.508
Take a look.

04:55.909 --> 04:57.345
YUKO:
Uh-huh.

04:57.378 --> 04:58.813
Impossible keeping up
with him.

05:07.054 --> 05:09.056
( laughing ):
Spheal.

05:09.089 --> 05:11.092
Wow, it's a Spheal.

05:11.125 --> 05:13.728
Spheal, Spheal.
Hi.

05:14.595 --> 05:16.831
Spheal, Spheal, Spheal.

05:16.864 --> 05:18.733
Spheal.

05:18.766 --> 05:22.703
Spheal, Spheal.
Spheal, Spheal.

05:22.736 --> 05:24.739
( laughs )

05:27.608 --> 05:29.544
Ah.

05:35.048 --> 05:36.784
( ominous theme playing )

05:47.895 --> 05:49.630
( roars )

06:00.841 --> 06:01.976
( panting )

06:02.009 --> 06:03.478
( both gasp )

06:07.114 --> 06:08.849
( explosion )

06:08.882 --> 06:10.985
( screaming )

06:15.022 --> 06:16.924
( creatures murmuring )

06:25.098 --> 06:26.734
( whimpering )

06:35.943 --> 06:37.445
ASH:
Tory?

06:41.782 --> 06:43.885
You're okay.
I've got you.

06:45.919 --> 06:48.456
Thank you, Daddy.

06:58.265 --> 07:01.202
( dramatic theme playing )

07:01.235 --> 07:02.703
( gasps )

07:23.891 --> 07:26.927
It's some kind of Pokémon,
isn't it?

07:26.960 --> 07:28.762
Yes. Hmm.

07:28.795 --> 07:31.833
It's a Pokémon from outer space.

07:57.124 --> 07:58.893
( roars )

08:20.881 --> 08:23.083
Rayquaza never leaves
the ozone layer.

08:23.116 --> 08:24.585
Why now?

08:33.093 --> 08:34.695
It regenerated.

08:34.728 --> 08:36.797
But how's that possible?

08:45.372 --> 08:47.141
Let's go.
It's too dangerous.

08:47.174 --> 08:48.643
Yeah.

08:59.052 --> 09:00.855
( roaring )

09:25.846 --> 09:27.781
Ah!
Are you okay?

09:27.814 --> 09:29.149
Huh?

09:29.182 --> 09:30.851
( electricity crackling )

09:46.333 --> 09:48.869
( roars )

09:50.871 --> 09:53.908
Quick, follow me.
I'm right behind you.

10:13.293 --> 10:14.996
Whoa!

10:17.330 --> 10:19.100
Ah!

10:26.006 --> 10:27.675
( roaring )

10:32.779 --> 10:35.916
SPHEAL:
Spheal, Spheal, Spheal, Spheal!

10:44.424 --> 10:47.861
( wailing )

10:47.894 --> 10:50.798
MAN 1: Oh, what is it?
MAN 2: Look at that.

10:50.831 --> 10:53.200
( both sigh )

11:03.276 --> 11:05.980
( roars )

11:21.828 --> 11:23.964
( dramatic theme playing )

11:35.542 --> 11:37.912
( wailing )

12:05.872 --> 12:08.008
LUND:
Rayquaza is furious.

12:09.242 --> 12:12.079
Another Pokémon crossing
into its territory

12:12.112 --> 12:14.081
has obviously threatened it.

12:37.504 --> 12:39.840
Huh?

12:45.078 --> 12:46.814
LUND:
Fire the laser.

12:59.559 --> 13:02.229
Raise our trajectory
by 0.5.

13:02.262 --> 13:04.098
Right.

13:10.237 --> 13:13.307
That's the frequency.
Finally, in sync.

13:13.340 --> 13:14.575
That means...?
Yes.

13:14.608 --> 13:19.113
The crystal should regenerate
if we keep the laser on target.

13:21.181 --> 13:24.351
We will succeed.
We have to.

13:43.937 --> 13:45.973
( alarm beeping )

13:49.576 --> 13:51.879
We overloaded the regulator.

13:59.953 --> 14:01.355
YUKO:
It was just one small component

14:01.388 --> 14:02.522
that malfunctioned.

14:02.555 --> 14:04.091
A simple replacement.

14:04.124 --> 14:05.659
LUND:
Good. We'll try again

14:05.692 --> 14:07.027
after it's fixed.

14:07.060 --> 14:08.362
YUKO:
Yes, sir.

14:08.395 --> 14:09.496
Huh?

14:09.529 --> 14:10.998
( laughs )

14:12.165 --> 14:14.101
Guess what?
I'm gonna tell you

14:14.134 --> 14:15.402
all about this book
I'm reading.

14:15.435 --> 14:16.637
It's so good.

14:16.670 --> 14:18.005
MAN 1:
Once that part's replaced,

14:18.038 --> 14:19.172
we're almost home.

14:19.205 --> 14:21.408
MAN 2:
Yeah, we're so close.

14:27.681 --> 14:30.951
I was right.
I did see it glow.

14:35.088 --> 14:37.424
( dramatic theme playing )

15:12.459 --> 15:14.728
BOTH:
Wow!

15:14.761 --> 15:17.097
WINGULL:
Wingull, Wingull, Wingull,

15:17.130 --> 15:21.201
Wingull, Wingull,
Wingull!

15:21.234 --> 15:24.037
PELIPPER:
Pelipper.

15:24.070 --> 15:26.340
 On his journey
to become a Pokémon master,

15:26.373 --> 15:29.242
 Ash Ketchum and his friends
arrive in Larousse City,

15:29.275 --> 15:32.512
 the headquarters for anything
and everything high-tech.

15:32.545 --> 15:35.282
 But he's not here
for the gadgets and gizmos.

15:35.315 --> 15:37.317
 Ash is itching for action

15:37.350 --> 15:40.087
 at the town's
famous Battle Tower.

15:41.087 --> 15:43.223
Pelipper.
Pelipper.

15:44.591 --> 15:46.160
Huh?

15:47.494 --> 15:49.330
( whimpering )

15:52.732 --> 15:54.501
( all panting )

15:57.370 --> 15:59.106
( panting )

16:02.642 --> 16:04.445
( squeals )

16:07.380 --> 16:09.316
( chattering )

16:21.694 --> 16:24.431
( both laughing )

16:24.464 --> 16:26.133
Yay!

16:31.805 --> 16:35.142
Munch. Munch.
Munch.

16:37.744 --> 16:39.380
( laughs )

16:48.621 --> 16:50.324
Munch.

16:53.827 --> 16:56.196
Munch.

16:57.664 --> 16:59.166
Munch.

17:04.337 --> 17:05.439
Munch.

17:07.440 --> 17:09.343
Munch.

17:10.777 --> 17:12.579
Munch.

17:25.859 --> 17:29.463
Munch. Munch.

17:38.872 --> 17:40.307
 Welcome.

17:40.340 --> 17:41.875
 You are now
in Larousse City.

17:41.908 --> 17:43.243
 Welcome again.

17:43.276 --> 17:45.112
Cool.
It's so cute.

17:45.145 --> 17:46.313
A robot.

17:46.346 --> 17:48.849
What could be better than that?
Pika.

17:48.882 --> 17:50.851
Being greeted by a real live
beautiful girl

17:50.884 --> 17:52.352
could be one thing.

17:53.820 --> 17:55.489
 Smile.

18:03.696 --> 18:05.699
 Visitor data confirmed.

18:05.732 --> 18:08.568
 Citizenship and point of origin
recorded.

18:08.601 --> 18:11.605
 These will serve
as your passports.

18:12.705 --> 18:13.840
Our passports?

18:13.873 --> 18:15.308
 While in Larousse City,

18:15.341 --> 18:16.877
 keep them with you
at all times.

18:16.910 --> 18:21.248
 Your passports can be used
for shopping and other needs.

18:24.817 --> 18:27.621
Don't think I'll be sending
this one home.

18:27.654 --> 18:30.624
So I wonder which way to go
for the Battle Tower.

18:30.657 --> 18:32.126
Pika.

18:33.259 --> 18:35.629
Help!
Pika!

18:37.664 --> 18:40.500
Hey, Ash,
quit messing around.

18:40.533 --> 18:42.469
A moving sidewalk.

18:46.206 --> 18:47.908
SID:
Dude, you're swimming upstream.

18:47.941 --> 18:50.377
There is an easier way.

18:50.410 --> 18:52.479
Well, if I ever get off
of this thing,

18:52.512 --> 18:53.880
then maybe you could show it
to me!

18:53.913 --> 18:55.615
Pika!

18:55.648 --> 18:56.883
Nice fall.

18:56.916 --> 18:58.619
Nice fall.

19:01.688 --> 19:02.856
Blaze.

19:02.889 --> 19:05.959
Help him out, Blaziken, okay?

19:05.992 --> 19:08.262
Blaze.

19:11.631 --> 19:14.535
Blaze. Blaze.

19:15.868 --> 19:17.804
Hey, thanks a lot.
Pikachu.

19:17.837 --> 19:19.539
Sure, no need to thank me.

19:19.572 --> 19:22.742
I just couldn't continue
watching you look like a fool.

19:22.775 --> 19:24.511
What?

19:24.544 --> 19:26.846
SID:
So I guess you're all new
in town, huh?

19:26.879 --> 19:29.349
RAFE:
Well, if you're heading
for the Battle Tower,

19:29.382 --> 19:30.784
you should try
going this way.

19:30.817 --> 19:34.254
AUDREY: Be careful.
KATHRYN: Don't fall.

19:34.287 --> 19:36.489
My name's Ash
from Pallet Town.

19:36.522 --> 19:38.225
How'd you like to battle
with me?

19:38.258 --> 19:40.827
Watch out,
my brother Rafe's really strong.

19:40.860 --> 19:43.296
Blaziken too.
Blaze.

19:43.329 --> 19:45.565
Yeah, I'd love to have
a battle with you, Ash.

19:45.598 --> 19:47.667
Let's get together
at the Battle Tower, okay?

19:47.700 --> 19:50.971
So we're finally gonna
settle this today, right, Rafe?

19:51.004 --> 19:53.306
Hello, my bespectacled beauty.

19:53.339 --> 19:55.242
I'm Brock.
Stop!

19:56.276 --> 19:58.011
Well, I guess you could say
that your friend here

19:58.044 --> 19:59.879
has really fallen
for Rebecca, huh?

19:59.912 --> 20:01.548
She's a good Metagross trainer,

20:01.581 --> 20:03.350
likes to use her laptop
for strategy.

20:03.383 --> 20:06.820
So my name is Sid.
Blastoise is my partner.

20:06.853 --> 20:08.321
Hi, I'm May.

20:08.354 --> 20:11.358
And this is my brother, Max.

20:11.391 --> 20:14.228
Hey, you're kind of cute.
Kind of?

20:15.528 --> 20:17.397
And kind of crazy too.

20:17.430 --> 20:19.666
Look, the Battle Tower.

20:21.367 --> 20:23.637
Look, Pikachu,
it's right there.

20:24.637 --> 20:27.541
I can't wait.
Pika.

20:31.344 --> 20:34.014
ASH:
I'll be back as soon
as I'm registered.

20:34.047 --> 20:36.416
MAX:
Okay, then we'll head
to the stands.

20:36.449 --> 20:37.718
ASH:
See you.

20:38.885 --> 20:40.554
There, let's hurry.

20:41.688 --> 20:42.789
( computer beeps )

20:44.023 --> 20:45.358
Ah.

20:45.391 --> 20:46.760
( laughs )

20:48.995 --> 20:51.665
Hmm. Uh-oh.

20:51.698 --> 20:53.267
Now where are we?

20:56.469 --> 20:59.473
Oh, wow, there's a library too.
Pika.

21:06.079 --> 21:08.548
Excuse me.
Pika!

21:09.849 --> 21:12.752
Hold on,
what do you running away for?

21:12.785 --> 21:13.920
Pika.

21:13.953 --> 21:16.556
Wait! Hold up!

21:19.926 --> 21:21.594
Hi. Let me start that again.

21:21.627 --> 21:22.862
We're on our way to a battle

21:22.895 --> 21:24.531
but we don't know
how to get there.

21:24.564 --> 21:27.701
So we're kind of lost.
Pika, Pika.

21:30.636 --> 21:33.373
Wait, we just wanna-- Hi.

21:33.406 --> 21:35.008
Are you ready for your battle?

21:35.041 --> 21:37.644
Right this way, gentlemen.

21:37.677 --> 21:39.412
But you don't understand.

21:39.445 --> 21:41.681
If you hurry up,
you two might just make it.

21:41.714 --> 21:43.583
But I haven't registered yet.

21:43.616 --> 21:45.919
That will all happen
automatically.

21:45.952 --> 21:47.688
Now, good luck, you two.

21:51.457 --> 21:52.959
COMPUTER:
 Passports confirmed.

21:52.992 --> 21:55.995
 Two youth-level participants
entered successfully.

21:56.028 --> 21:58.899
Great, and just in time.
Pika.

22:00.867 --> 22:04.437
 Entry for participants
in the first round is closed.

22:04.470 --> 22:06.106
 Please try again next time.

22:06.139 --> 22:07.607
What?

22:08.741 --> 22:11.611
 Now introducing
our first entry.

22:15.114 --> 22:16.750
Pika.

22:19.886 --> 22:22.756
Here we go.
Pikachu.

22:26.692 --> 22:29.028
ANNOUNCER:
 Our first match will be
an official

22:29.061 --> 22:30.697
 Battle Tower tag team event.

22:30.730 --> 22:32.999
 Remember to cheer
for your favorites.

22:33.032 --> 22:35.435
Tag team, huh? Yeah.

22:35.468 --> 22:37.704
 We have Ash Ketchum
in the blue corner,

22:37.737 --> 22:39.939
 a trainer all the way
from Pallet Town.

22:39.972 --> 22:43.076
 And his tag partner Tory,
a local trainer.

22:43.109 --> 22:44.778
All right, Tory, good luck.

22:44.811 --> 22:48.148
I wonder how Ash
got entered so quickly.

22:48.181 --> 22:50.016
By cutting in front of me.

22:50.049 --> 22:51.618
Rebecca,

22:51.651 --> 22:53.052
there comes a time
in a man's life

22:53.085 --> 22:55.755
when he's presented with
the gift of love at first sight.

22:55.788 --> 22:59.693
How about pain at first pull?
Not the ear.

23:01.227 --> 23:05.165
Professor Lund,
take a look at this.

23:05.198 --> 23:07.834
Tory?
In a Pokémon battle?

23:09.168 --> 23:10.670
 And in the red corner,

23:10.703 --> 23:12.906
 we have two trainers
from South City,

23:12.939 --> 23:14.607
 Rafe and Sid.

23:14.640 --> 23:17.477
Hey, Ash,
you sure didn't waste any time.

23:19.645 --> 23:21.881
Of course not,
I couldn't wait to beat you.

23:21.914 --> 23:23.550
Hey! May!

23:23.583 --> 23:24.918
Make sure you watch.

23:24.951 --> 23:27.487
I'm dedicating this battle
to you.

23:29.956 --> 23:32.926
 The basic rule in all tag team
battles is teamwork.

23:32.959 --> 23:35.228
 Each trainer uses a single
Pokémon

23:35.261 --> 23:36.796
 and works with his teammate.

23:36.829 --> 23:40.900
 And now, trainers,
bring out your Pokémon.

23:40.933 --> 23:43.737
All right. Here goes.
Here goes.

23:46.272 --> 23:48.942
Blaze.
Blastoise.

23:48.975 --> 23:50.977
Pikachu, I choose you.

23:51.010 --> 23:53.012
Pika. Pikachu.

23:53.045 --> 23:55.515
Tory, what Pokémon
are you gonna use?

23:55.548 --> 23:57.550
No, Ash,
I don't have any Pokémon.

23:57.583 --> 23:58.785
But...
Pika.

23:58.818 --> 24:00.687
 There seems to be a problem.

24:00.720 --> 24:02.689
 We've seen only one Pokémon
from the blue corner.

24:02.722 --> 24:04.858
See, I was trying
to tell you.

24:04.891 --> 24:07.560
I'm not a trainer.
I can't battle.

24:07.593 --> 24:08.795
But this could end up

24:08.828 --> 24:10.797
being my only chance
to battle Rafe.

24:10.830 --> 24:13.867
Hey, I know what,
I'll loan you one of my Pokémon.

24:13.900 --> 24:14.901
What do you say?

24:14.934 --> 24:16.870
Come on, that'll work.
But...

24:18.170 --> 24:20.106
 Will the blue corner forfeit?

24:20.139 --> 24:22.675
Don't let me down, Tory.

24:22.708 --> 24:25.011
Well, if I have to.

24:27.146 --> 24:29.949
Torkoal.

24:29.982 --> 24:32.719
 So looks like
we have our Pokémon.

24:32.752 --> 24:35.088
 Ready for a battle,
because here we go!

24:35.121 --> 24:38.258
Let's do it.
Blaziken, use Blaze Kick now.

24:38.291 --> 24:42.161
Blaziken.

24:42.194 --> 24:44.130
Dodge, Pikachu.

24:44.163 --> 24:45.765
Pika.

24:47.166 --> 24:48.801
Go, Blastoise, Hydro Pump.

24:48.834 --> 24:51.771
Blastoise.
Pika!

24:51.804 --> 24:54.741
 It's a dazzling combination
from the red corner.

24:54.774 --> 24:57.811
Blastoise, Bubble Attack.
Blastoise.

24:59.979 --> 25:03.650
Torkoal. Tory, you have to tell
Torkoal to do something.

25:03.683 --> 25:05.585
But I don't know
what to tell it.

25:05.618 --> 25:09.155
Blastoise, Rapid Spin.
Blastoise.

25:09.188 --> 25:12.058
Blastoise!

25:14.860 --> 25:17.731
Torkoal!

25:18.831 --> 25:21.034
Blast.

25:22.168 --> 25:23.737
( breathing heavily )

25:32.244 --> 25:34.014
Blastoise.

25:35.214 --> 25:37.350
Blastoise.

25:37.383 --> 25:40.887
Pikachu, use Thunderbolt.
Cover Torkoal.

25:40.920 --> 25:42.889
Pikachu!

25:42.922 --> 25:47.360
Blastoise.
Blaziken.

25:47.393 --> 25:49.329
Blastoise, Skull Bash, go.

25:49.362 --> 25:50.930
Blastoise.

25:50.963 --> 25:53.066
Torkoal.

25:53.099 --> 25:55.001
Torkoal.
 Looks like the blue corner

25:55.034 --> 25:57.804
 just can't seem to get it
together as a team.

25:57.837 --> 26:00.006
Man, Ash's partner
isn't doing anything

26:00.039 --> 26:01.007
to help him out at all.

26:01.040 --> 26:03.343
I don't see how he could win.

26:03.376 --> 26:05.812
Come on, do something.

26:07.079 --> 26:09.215
Tory, don't worry,
I'll take care of it.

26:09.248 --> 26:11.117
Flamethrower, Torkoal, go.

26:11.150 --> 26:12.285
Torkoal.
Pika.

26:12.318 --> 26:15.121
Torkoal!

26:15.154 --> 26:17.757
 Oh, a Flamethrower
from Torkoal,

26:17.790 --> 26:19.225
 but it hit Pikachu.

26:19.258 --> 26:22.028
Torkoal, Torkoal.

26:22.061 --> 26:22.895
How embarrassing.

26:22.929 --> 26:25.832
So, Rafe,
wanna finish this one up?

26:25.865 --> 26:28.668
Let's go. Blaziken, Overheat.

26:28.701 --> 26:30.737
Blaziken!

26:30.770 --> 26:35.241
Pika! Pika!

26:35.274 --> 26:37.010
Pikachu, Torkoal.

26:37.043 --> 26:38.711
 And that's it.

26:38.744 --> 26:40.913
 Pikachu and Torkoal
are unable to battle.

26:40.946 --> 26:45.652
 Rafe and Sid are the winners.
Congratulations.

26:47.153 --> 26:50.189
Blaze.
Blastoise.

26:50.222 --> 26:52.258
( laughs )

26:52.291 --> 26:53.994
( elevator dings )

26:58.431 --> 27:00.900
Tory.
Daddy.

27:00.933 --> 27:02.802
We just watched
your Pokémon battle.

27:02.835 --> 27:04.070
I'm incredibly proud.

27:04.103 --> 27:06.673
Don't be.
It was all an accident,

27:06.706 --> 27:09.042
wasn't even supposed to happen.

27:11.043 --> 27:12.178
ALL:
Huh?

27:17.416 --> 27:20.820
Yuko, meeting you reminds me
of a time in my life

27:20.853 --> 27:22.455
when I too spent long hours

27:22.488 --> 27:24.157
toiling as a professor's
assistant.

27:24.190 --> 27:26.392
I'm sure Professor Ivy
would be happy

27:26.425 --> 27:28.161
to vouch for my work.

27:28.194 --> 27:31.197
And I'll be happy to vouch
for his insanity.

27:32.765 --> 27:35.201
We apologize for the mix-up
with your battle.

27:35.234 --> 27:36.402
The truth is,

27:36.435 --> 27:38.905
Tory is completely afraid
of Pokémon.

27:38.938 --> 27:40.973
How could he be afraid
of Pokémon?

27:41.006 --> 27:43.409
Well, about four years ago,

27:43.442 --> 27:45.778
he had a very traumatic
experience

27:45.811 --> 27:48.081
and it left him terrified
of them.

27:48.114 --> 27:52.218
Sadly, he still hasn't managed
to get over those fears.

28:23.516 --> 28:26.185
Wow, I shouldn't have pushed him
so hard.

28:26.218 --> 28:29.155
But underneath it all,
I think he loves them.

28:29.188 --> 28:31.224
All he really needs
is the chance

28:31.257 --> 28:33.226
to get to know them,
that's all.

28:33.259 --> 28:35.495
I'm sure that's all it'll take.

28:35.528 --> 28:38.831
Fine. Then I'll give him
that chance.

28:38.864 --> 28:40.800
All he needs now
is to become friends

28:40.833 --> 28:41.968
with me and Pikachu.

28:42.001 --> 28:44.937
Right, pal?
Pika.

28:44.970 --> 28:46.939
I wanna help too.
So do I.

28:46.972 --> 28:48.341
Me too.
Cool.

28:48.374 --> 28:50.910
So, what do you say we all go
and look for Tory, okay?

28:50.943 --> 28:52.078
ALL:
Yeah!

28:52.111 --> 28:54.847
You're awful kind.
Thank you.

28:54.880 --> 28:56.883
( whimpering )

28:58.384 --> 28:59.919
( grunts )

29:06.125 --> 29:09.062
ASH: Tory?
PIKACHU: Pika?

29:13.933 --> 29:15.802
( both chattering )

29:17.570 --> 29:19.105
( both squeal )

29:21.106 --> 29:22.308
( laughs )

29:28.180 --> 29:29.348
Later.

29:29.381 --> 29:31.785
Pika.

29:33.352 --> 29:35.321
( both chattering )

29:40.860 --> 29:44.998
Munch. Munch.

29:52.338 --> 29:54.874
Munch. Munch.

30:00.246 --> 30:01.881
Munch.

30:07.386 --> 30:09.088
Munch.

30:22.501 --> 30:25.004
TORY:
Hey, come on out.

30:25.037 --> 30:26.205
Where are you?

30:26.238 --> 30:29.108
I wanna tell you
something important.

30:35.514 --> 30:37.016
( laughs )

30:43.255 --> 30:45.024
You'll never guess
what I just did.

30:45.057 --> 30:46.559
I helped out a Pokémon.

30:46.592 --> 30:48.895
Because it had its head stuck
inside a garbage can

30:48.928 --> 30:50.496
and so I helped to get it out.

30:50.529 --> 30:52.231
Isn't that cool?

30:52.264 --> 30:54.434
( laughing )

30:58.637 --> 31:01.207
( dramatic theme playing )

31:28.033 --> 31:30.169
( both panting )

31:35.341 --> 31:37.076
( all gasp )

31:41.146 --> 31:44.350
Hey, what are those lights?

31:44.383 --> 31:47.253
And I was even part
of a Pokémon battle too.

31:47.286 --> 31:50.556
Of course, I wasn't very good,
so that part kind of stunk.

31:50.589 --> 31:53.693
ASH:
Hey, who are you talking to?

31:53.726 --> 31:55.295
Pika.

32:06.472 --> 32:09.075
Hey, it's gone.

32:11.076 --> 32:14.347
Come on, who was it?
None of your business.

32:14.380 --> 32:15.681
Why, would it hurt
to tell me?

32:15.714 --> 32:19.118
Stop.
Leave me alone, okay?

32:19.151 --> 32:20.586
( grunting )
Wait a minute.

32:20.619 --> 32:22.455
If this town
is so high-tech,

32:22.488 --> 32:24.423
why don't they
have moving sidewalks?

32:24.456 --> 32:26.726
Or robots
that serve hamburgers?

32:26.759 --> 32:28.561
Yeah, keep dreaming.

32:28.594 --> 32:32.365
( all groaning )

32:32.398 --> 32:34.333
BOY:
I'll take a hamburger, please.

32:34.366 --> 32:36.302
 Hamburger.

32:41.240 --> 32:42.508
Yum.

32:43.642 --> 32:45.311
( all laugh )

32:45.344 --> 32:47.279
ALL:
Hamburgers, please.

32:47.312 --> 32:49.582
 Passport. Passport.
Passport.

32:49.615 --> 32:51.083
What's a passport?

32:51.116 --> 32:52.718
Well, I have no idea
what kind of pass

32:52.751 --> 32:54.186
he's talking about.

32:54.219 --> 32:56.522
But, Meowth,
please stop calling me sport.

32:56.555 --> 32:58.524
You idiot. Hamburger!

32:58.557 --> 33:02.161
Hey, that ain't right.
Cheeseburger!

33:02.194 --> 33:04.330
 Alert. Alert. Alert.
Now, now, now!

33:07.533 --> 33:09.502
( Meowth grunting )
JESSIE: Come on! Come on!

33:09.535 --> 33:12.071
 Come on, come on.
( Jessie screaming )

33:12.104 --> 33:14.473
That was rude.
Maybe she takes our order?

33:14.506 --> 33:18.244
Yeah? Well, I'm pretty good
at giving orders.

33:18.277 --> 33:21.447
So I'm gonna have
five hamburgers well-done

33:21.480 --> 33:23.449
and don't forget
the french fries.

33:23.482 --> 33:24.784
 Well done, it is.

33:24.817 --> 33:27.253
( screaming )

33:27.286 --> 33:28.821
Jessie got fried!

33:28.854 --> 33:31.090
Without the burgers.

33:31.123 --> 33:34.160
I think we should battle
together again.

33:34.193 --> 33:36.095
Bet we'll get it right
next time.

33:36.128 --> 33:38.697
Why do you keep following me?

33:38.730 --> 33:40.533
WINGULL:
Gull. Gull. Wingull.

33:40.566 --> 33:42.135
Ah!

33:43.335 --> 33:46.105
Are you okay?
Pikachu?

33:46.138 --> 33:48.207
Ah!
Pika.

33:49.408 --> 33:51.143
Gee, thanks.

33:51.176 --> 33:52.845
Why'd you have to go
and push me?

33:52.878 --> 33:56.082
MAY:
Ash, stop.

33:56.115 --> 33:58.584
Don't start something.
Okay.

34:00.586 --> 34:02.621
Oh! Oh!

34:02.654 --> 34:04.723
Hey, I know.

34:04.756 --> 34:06.358
Pika.

34:06.391 --> 34:08.494
( upbeat theme playing )

34:13.699 --> 34:16.435
Hmm. Perfect. Dig in.

34:16.468 --> 34:17.770
I'll go first.

34:17.803 --> 34:20.806
Second.
Hold on.

34:20.839 --> 34:23.342
Whoa, it's hot.

34:23.375 --> 34:24.343
Yum.

34:24.376 --> 34:26.779
There's nothing that can stop
an argument

34:26.812 --> 34:28.581
better than a bunch
of full mouths.

34:28.614 --> 34:32.085
Try some, Tory,
it's really good.

34:39.758 --> 34:41.694
You're right.
Told you so.

34:41.727 --> 34:43.662
( all laughing )

34:43.695 --> 34:46.232
ASH:
Guys, look at
all those Pokémon.

34:46.265 --> 34:47.633
SEEDOT:
Seedot.

34:47.666 --> 34:49.268
Well, hi.

34:49.301 --> 34:52.338
There's plenty of Pokémon food
so don't be shy.

34:52.371 --> 34:54.640
There. Dig in, guys.
Seedot.

34:54.673 --> 34:57.443
Seedot. Seedot. Seedot.

34:57.476 --> 35:00.679
Tory, don't you think
they're the cutest?

35:00.712 --> 35:02.248
Yeah.
Hey,

35:02.281 --> 35:03.749
I bet they'd
let you pet them.

35:03.782 --> 35:05.384
Pika.
( gasps )

35:05.417 --> 35:07.120
Pika.

35:09.788 --> 35:11.357
( grunts )

35:11.390 --> 35:12.658
( gasping )
Pika?

35:15.460 --> 35:18.264
Thanks, guys. I'm sorry.

35:19.198 --> 35:21.500
Well, we tried.
Pika.

35:21.533 --> 35:24.303
I'm sure we'll get through
to him eventually.

35:24.336 --> 35:25.905
Seedot. Seedot.
Oh, guys!

35:25.938 --> 35:27.406
Munch. Munch. Munch.

35:28.574 --> 35:29.609
( all gasp )

35:29.642 --> 35:32.378
Oh, no, it's a Munchlax,
and they love to eat.

35:32.411 --> 35:35.447
Well, guess
it's doing what it loves.

35:35.480 --> 35:38.551
Hey, you,
that was our lunch.

35:43.589 --> 35:44.690
Munch!

35:45.958 --> 35:48.794
Munch. Munch. Munch.

35:48.827 --> 35:50.296
Munch.

35:51.230 --> 35:52.531
ALL:
Wow.

35:52.564 --> 35:55.267
Hey, it's a Plusle
and Minun.

35:55.300 --> 35:56.602
Hi, cuties.

35:56.635 --> 35:58.370
Pika. Pika.

35:58.403 --> 36:01.574
( both chattering )

36:01.607 --> 36:03.542
Pika. Pika.

36:03.575 --> 36:06.479
PELIPPERS:
Pelipper. Pelipper.

36:11.416 --> 36:13.919
MURKROWS:
Murkrow. Murkrow. Murkrow.

36:13.952 --> 36:16.489
( suspenseful theme playing )

36:17.990 --> 36:20.626
Murkrow. Murkrow. Murkrow.

36:23.528 --> 36:27.466
( explosion )
( Murkrows shouting )

36:43.482 --> 36:45.351
( dramatic theme playing )

37:10.442 --> 37:12.511
MAX:
There's that light
in the sky again.

37:12.544 --> 37:13.545
Awesome.

37:13.578 --> 37:15.614
Pika.
It's beautiful.

37:15.647 --> 37:18.384
Well, but that's impossible.

37:18.417 --> 37:21.353
What is?
That's called an aurora,

37:21.386 --> 37:22.588
but it can only be seen

37:22.621 --> 37:24.757
at the north
and the south poles.

37:24.790 --> 37:26.425
Strange.

37:26.458 --> 37:27.826
Well, then I guess,

37:27.859 --> 37:30.062
we're lucky to be able
to see it here, right?

37:30.095 --> 37:31.563
The same kind of luck

37:31.596 --> 37:34.500
that brought you
and me together, right, babe?

37:34.533 --> 37:36.869
Not sure what kind of luck
that was.

37:36.902 --> 37:38.337
Hi, beautiful.

37:38.370 --> 37:40.773
If you're looking
for a real phenomenon,

37:40.806 --> 37:44.076
stop looking in your computer
and spend some time with me.

37:44.109 --> 37:49.782
Okay, you leaving her alone,
that's a phenomenon.

37:49.815 --> 37:52.651
Well, look who's still in town.
So?

37:52.684 --> 37:54.553
Well, after
that devastating defeat

37:54.586 --> 37:55.854
in front
of thousands of people,

37:55.887 --> 37:57.656
I thought you might be
a little embarrassed

37:57.689 --> 37:59.558
to show your face.
Oh, yeah?

37:59.591 --> 38:02.661
How about a rematch tomorrow
in the Battle Tower?

38:02.694 --> 38:03.495
No problem.

38:03.528 --> 38:06.732
I'll beat you anytime
and anywhere.

38:06.765 --> 38:09.769
I wouldn't count on that.
Pika.

38:11.136 --> 38:14.707
Hey, I know you.
Tory.

38:16.541 --> 38:21.347
Hey, you guys.
Yuko and I made these for you.

38:21.380 --> 38:23.115
MAX:
Cool. Pokémon cookies.

38:23.148 --> 38:24.717
KATHRYN: Cute.
AUDREY: Yummy.

38:24.750 --> 38:26.618
ASH:
Come on out, everyone.

38:26.651 --> 38:28.787
( Bree Sharp's "The Side
of Paradise" playing )

38:28.820 --> 38:31.357
 ♪ La, la, la, la, la ♪

38:31.390 --> 38:32.958
 ♪ La, la, la, la
La, la, la ♪

38:32.991 --> 38:36.028
 ♪ La, la, la, la, la ♪

38:36.061 --> 38:37.563
 ♪ La, la, la, la, la, la ♪

38:38.730 --> 38:40.032
( grunting )

38:40.065 --> 38:42.034
 ♪ There's a place I know ♪

38:42.067 --> 38:44.036
 ♪ It's always jumping ♪

38:44.069 --> 38:45.437
 ♪ I'm thinking
We should go ♪

38:45.470 --> 38:48.607
 ♪ And leave our worries ♪

38:48.640 --> 38:50.409
 ♪ You got a friend in me ♪

38:50.442 --> 38:52.578
 ♪ And I'll tell you
Something ♪

38:52.611 --> 38:56.648
 ♪ This time
Could be extraordinary ♪

38:56.681 --> 39:00.853
 ♪ When shadows fall
You're feeling small ♪

39:00.886 --> 39:05.124
 ♪ It looks like walls
Are closing in ♪

39:05.157 --> 39:06.458
 ♪ Don't be afraid ♪

39:06.491 --> 39:08.093
 ♪ The dark will fade ♪

39:08.126 --> 39:10.095
 ♪ Just take my hand ♪

39:10.128 --> 39:12.431
 ♪ And look again ♪

39:12.464 --> 39:14.733
 ♪ This side of paradise ♪

39:14.766 --> 39:16.468
 ♪ Is where I want to be ♪

39:16.501 --> 39:18.937
 ♪ This side of paradise ♪

39:18.970 --> 39:20.639
 ♪ For you and me ♪

39:20.672 --> 39:22.841
 ♪ This side of paradise ♪

39:22.874 --> 39:24.777
 ♪ What you get
Is what you see ♪

39:24.810 --> 39:28.947
 ♪ And I never thought
I'd see a place as nice ♪

39:28.980 --> 39:30.616
 ♪ This side of paradise ♪

39:30.649 --> 39:32.151
 ♪ La, la, la, la, la ♪

39:32.184 --> 39:34.052
 ♪ La, la, la, la, la, la ♪

39:34.085 --> 39:36.588
 ♪ La, la, la, la, la ♪

39:36.621 --> 39:38.757
 ♪ La, la, la, la, la ♪

39:38.790 --> 39:43.028
 ♪ Forget about the pain
And doubt ♪

39:43.061 --> 39:47.633
 ♪ Your happiness is overdue ♪

39:47.666 --> 39:49.168
 ♪ I've been dreaming of ♪

39:49.201 --> 39:50.903
 ♪ Dream ♪
 ♪ The skies above ♪

39:50.936 --> 39:54.039
 ♪ Dancing through the stars
With you ♪

39:54.072 --> 39:58.444
 ♪ Oh, take me to ♪

39:58.477 --> 40:01.046
 ♪ This side of paradise ♪

40:01.079 --> 40:02.681
 ♪ Is where I want to be ♪

40:02.714 --> 40:05.050
 ♪ This side of paradise ♪

40:05.083 --> 40:06.452
 ♪ For you and me ♪

40:06.485 --> 40:09.455
 ♪ This side of paradise ♪

40:09.488 --> 40:11.123
 ♪ What you get
Is what you see ♪

40:11.156 --> 40:14.760
 ♪ This side of paradise ♪

40:16.695 --> 40:19.164
When is a sandwich
more than a sandwich?

40:19.197 --> 40:23.101
When the sandwich is a meal--
For Team Rocket to steal.

40:23.134 --> 40:24.837
Dinner.
Dinner.

40:26.972 --> 40:28.941
ALL:
Ah!

40:28.974 --> 40:30.843
Huh?

40:30.876 --> 40:32.678
Munch. Munch.

40:32.711 --> 40:34.980
Did that just happen?
Munch. Munch. Munch.

40:36.114 --> 40:37.649
Munch. Munch. Munch.

40:37.682 --> 40:39.685
It's stealing the food
we were stealing.

40:39.718 --> 40:40.986
Oh, no, it's not.

40:41.019 --> 40:42.821
( growls )

40:42.854 --> 40:44.823
Munch. Munch. Munch.
JESSIE: Carry all--

40:44.856 --> 40:47.593
( all grumbling indistinctly )

40:52.664 --> 40:54.767
It's gone.

40:55.834 --> 40:57.503
( ominous theme playing )

41:12.050 --> 41:14.019
( roars )

41:23.895 --> 41:26.198
TORY:
You know, I've never
done that before.

41:26.231 --> 41:27.733
What?

41:27.766 --> 41:30.569
Just playing together
with a big bunch of friends.

41:30.602 --> 41:32.137
Really?
Yeah.

41:32.170 --> 41:34.006
I guess it's because
I've always been

41:34.039 --> 41:36.909
so afraid of Pokémon.

41:36.942 --> 41:40.712
So I'm afraid to get close
to Pokémon trainers too.

41:40.745 --> 41:43.615
Guess I've missed out on a lot.
Hmm.

41:43.648 --> 41:45.784
That means
you're always alone.

41:45.817 --> 41:47.019
Pika.

41:48.186 --> 41:49.688
Pikachu.

41:49.721 --> 41:51.323
But that's all
in the past, right?

41:51.356 --> 41:52.958
Pika.

41:57.062 --> 41:58.531
Hmm.

42:04.736 --> 42:06.672
Corphish!
( screams )

42:06.705 --> 42:08.106
Corphish!
Corphish!

42:08.139 --> 42:09.274
Corphish!

42:09.307 --> 42:11.810
It's okay.

42:11.843 --> 42:14.780
There's no rush.
Okay.

42:14.813 --> 42:16.915
That's Corphish.

42:16.948 --> 42:18.317
Cor...

42:18.350 --> 42:20.920
Pika.
...phish.

42:23.388 --> 42:26.191
TORY:
Come on, guys, there's someone
I want you to meet.

42:26.224 --> 42:27.759
We are we going?

42:27.792 --> 42:29.661
Wherever it is,
I hope there's a kitchen.

42:29.694 --> 42:30.963
( chuckles ):
I'm starving.

42:37.702 --> 42:40.673
 Your passports, please.

42:42.974 --> 42:44.076
 Verified.

42:45.910 --> 42:48.046
My dad's lab
is right over there

42:48.079 --> 42:51.116
so that's why there are so many
security robots all over.

42:59.658 --> 43:00.959
Come on out.

43:00.992 --> 43:05.598
I'm with my new friends.
Come and meet them.

43:10.001 --> 43:13.405
Pika.
So this is your friend, Tory?

43:13.438 --> 43:14.973
But what is it?

43:15.006 --> 43:17.242
It's gorgeous.
And weird.

43:17.275 --> 43:20.379
It's always here for me
whenever I call for it.

43:20.412 --> 43:22.648
Yesterday,
I played with all these guys

43:22.681 --> 43:24.082
and their Pokémon too.

43:24.115 --> 43:25.350
ALL:
Wow!

43:25.383 --> 43:27.319
Wow, Tory, that's so cool.

43:27.352 --> 43:29.221
And it even understands
what I say.

43:29.254 --> 43:30.889
MAY:
Is it a Pokémon?

43:30.922 --> 43:32.658
MAX:
Not one that I've ever seen.

43:32.691 --> 43:34.760
This is just fascinating.

43:34.793 --> 43:37.262
What do you say
I introduce my Pokémon to it?

43:37.295 --> 43:39.198
Go!

43:41.266 --> 43:42.401
Blaze.

43:42.434 --> 43:44.002
Yeah, mine too.

43:44.035 --> 43:45.671
BOTH:
Don't forget ours.

43:47.439 --> 43:49.274
Masquerain.
Blastoise.

43:49.307 --> 43:51.877
Now, let me introduce mine.

43:53.311 --> 43:54.746
Metagross.

43:54.779 --> 43:57.015
A Metagross. Awesome.

43:57.048 --> 43:58.183
Meta.

43:58.216 --> 44:00.185
Pika.
( giggles )

44:02.487 --> 44:04.189
Blast.
Blaze.

44:06.891 --> 44:08.694
Whoa.
( all chuckling )

44:12.063 --> 44:14.166
I got you!

44:14.199 --> 44:16.868
Missed it.

44:16.901 --> 44:18.403
Pika.

44:18.436 --> 44:20.305
Pi--
Whoa!

44:20.338 --> 44:21.907
Oh!
Pi--

44:23.508 --> 44:25.811
( wind roaring )

44:30.482 --> 44:32.918
( howls )

44:36.221 --> 44:37.189
( emergency alarm beeps )

44:37.222 --> 44:39.758
Unidentified object
approaching the building.

44:39.791 --> 44:42.094
Can you
analyze it, please?

44:43.361 --> 44:45.163
It appears to be a Rayquaza.

44:45.196 --> 44:46.097
Rayquaza?

44:46.131 --> 44:49.234
Contact Professor Lund now.
MAN: Right.

44:53.071 --> 44:56.208
Professor, how could a Rayquaza
be coming here?

44:56.241 --> 44:57.743
I don't know.

44:57.776 --> 44:59.811
But for it to leave
the ozone layer again,

44:59.844 --> 45:02.247
there must be
a powerful reason.

45:03.882 --> 45:05.718
( computers beeping )

45:09.220 --> 45:11.323
Do you see that?

45:11.356 --> 45:12.491
I'll magnify it.

45:12.524 --> 45:14.827
( suspenseful theme playing )

45:15.994 --> 45:17.362
That's what I thought.

45:17.395 --> 45:19.364
It's Deoxys.

45:19.397 --> 45:21.734
( ominous theme playing )

45:31.476 --> 45:33.044
COMPUTER:
 System malfunction.

45:33.077 --> 45:35.814
 Losing regulatory control.

45:38.950 --> 45:40.352
LUND:
 Rayquaza must have come here

45:40.385 --> 45:43.121
 after sensing that Deoxys
was here as well.

45:43.154 --> 45:45.791
 If those two battle it out
in our city,

45:45.824 --> 45:47.292
 the result
will be catastrophic.

45:47.325 --> 45:50.395
 Evacuate Larousse City
immediately.

45:50.428 --> 45:53.098
Right away, sir.

45:53.131 --> 45:56.034
Initiating
emergency evacuation.

45:59.070 --> 46:00.338
JENNY ( over P.A. ):
 Fellow citizens,

46:00.371 --> 46:02.974
 we are facing
an emergency situation.

46:03.007 --> 46:05.010
 Please evacuate immediately.

46:05.043 --> 46:07.546
( indistinct chattering )

46:07.579 --> 46:08.947
MAN:
It's party time.

46:08.980 --> 46:11.082
 Please be patient.

46:11.115 --> 46:13.952
 The next ferry
will arrive shortly.

46:18.356 --> 46:20.359
( indistinct chattering )

46:24.062 --> 46:26.331
( alarm blaring )

46:29.934 --> 46:33.305
What's that?
It sounds like the police.

46:33.338 --> 46:34.940
ALL:
Huh?

46:38.076 --> 46:39.578
Tory's out in the garden.

46:39.611 --> 46:42.080
I have to go out
and get him.

46:42.113 --> 46:44.249
Everyone,
evacuate immediately.

46:44.282 --> 46:45.384
Right.

46:52.891 --> 46:54.593
Why won't your
passport work?

46:54.626 --> 46:56.161
This never happens.

46:56.194 --> 46:57.929
Maybe, the system
is shutting down.

46:57.962 --> 47:00.098
( all gasp )

47:01.466 --> 47:03.201
Huh?

47:03.234 --> 47:05.270
It stopped.

47:05.303 --> 47:06.471
 Rebooting.

47:06.504 --> 47:08.207
( grunts )

47:14.345 --> 47:16.147
( grunts )

47:16.180 --> 47:17.148
MAN:
Hey!

47:17.181 --> 47:18.851
( speaking indistinctly )

47:34.599 --> 47:37.302
WOMAN 1: It's moving.
WOMAN 2: Where are we going?

47:37.335 --> 47:38.904
( girl gasps )

47:38.937 --> 47:41.973
WOMAN 3: Excuse me.
MAN: Watch it.

47:42.006 --> 47:44.409
( screams )

47:47.312 --> 47:49.247
Professor Lund.

47:49.280 --> 47:51.249
Ah.

47:51.282 --> 47:52.918
MEOWTH:
Oh, some vacation

47:52.951 --> 47:54.119
this turned out to be.

47:54.152 --> 47:56.221
JESSIE:
Whose bad idea was this?

47:56.254 --> 47:58.189
JAMES:
Let's just say Meowth and I
were overruled.

47:58.222 --> 47:59.491
JESSIE AND MEOWTH:
Huh?

48:11.436 --> 48:13.272
Hey!

48:14.706 --> 48:17.042
( suspenseful theme playing )

48:20.979 --> 48:22.380
What's happening here?

48:22.413 --> 48:25.317
Those things
are carrying people away.

48:25.350 --> 48:28.586
Deoxys, why are you doing
this to us?

48:28.619 --> 48:30.422
( Raybuaza howls )
Huh?

48:30.455 --> 48:32.424
( roars )

48:51.743 --> 48:53.311
The force field.

48:53.344 --> 48:55.480
( dramatic theme playing )

49:08.159 --> 49:09.461
COMPUTER:
 Losing power.

49:09.494 --> 49:12.497
 All systems
will now shut down.

49:22.106 --> 49:23.508
( roars )

49:40.091 --> 49:42.627
( roaring )

49:42.660 --> 49:44.997
( grunts )

49:47.665 --> 49:51.302
Blastoise. Blas--

49:51.335 --> 49:54.306
Blastoise.

49:55.406 --> 49:57.342
Blastoise.

49:57.375 --> 49:58.610
( grunts )

49:58.643 --> 50:01.112
BOTH:
You got it.

50:01.145 --> 50:03.015
Hold on a sec.

50:07.552 --> 50:08.787
It's multiplying.

50:08.820 --> 50:11.623
What is that thing?
Deoxys.

50:11.656 --> 50:12.791
You know its name?

50:12.824 --> 50:14.125
You guys, come back.

50:14.158 --> 50:15.660
ALL:
Huh?

50:15.693 --> 50:17.562
( all gasp )

50:17.595 --> 50:19.264
No, May, look out.

50:19.297 --> 50:20.832
Hey, what do you want?

50:20.865 --> 50:23.368
Blastoise,
use Hydro Pump. Go!

50:23.401 --> 50:25.237
Blastoise!

50:30.408 --> 50:33.445
Blastoise.
Put me down.

50:33.478 --> 50:36.281
Blastoise! Blast!

50:36.314 --> 50:39.418
Sid, no!
May, get in here.

50:40.318 --> 50:43.421
Blaziken, use Flamethrower.

50:43.454 --> 50:46.424
Blaze.

50:46.457 --> 50:48.460
ASH:
Pikachu, Thunderbolt.

50:48.493 --> 50:50.562
PIKACHU:
Pikachu!

50:53.131 --> 50:54.866
Tory, is there
another way out?

50:54.899 --> 50:57.368
Yeah, there is
an underground exit.

50:57.401 --> 50:59.704
Can you show us?
Yes, follow me.

50:59.737 --> 51:01.840
Everyone, let's go.

51:01.873 --> 51:04.609
( suspenseful theme playing )

51:04.642 --> 51:07.212
Blaze!

51:08.379 --> 51:10.115
( screams )

51:10.915 --> 51:12.450
Blaze!

51:12.483 --> 51:15.120
Way to go, Rafe.
All in a day's work.

51:19.223 --> 51:20.492
What do they want?

51:28.533 --> 51:29.567
Let's hurry.

51:29.600 --> 51:32.604
Come on, Brock, it's open.
Okay.

51:32.637 --> 51:35.474
All right, Ash, Rafe,
we gotta go.

51:36.941 --> 51:39.477
Pikachu.
Pika.

51:39.510 --> 51:41.313
( grunts )

51:42.613 --> 51:44.616
Blaze.

51:44.649 --> 51:46.351
Guys, this way.

51:51.355 --> 51:53.592
( panting )
Pika?

51:55.359 --> 51:56.528
Pika!
( all grunt )

51:56.561 --> 51:58.930
Pikachu,
use Thunderbolt now.

51:58.963 --> 52:01.533
Pikachu!

52:03.401 --> 52:07.505
Thanks, Pikachu.
Good Thunderbolt.

52:07.538 --> 52:09.474
Ash, what are you doing?
Let's go.

52:09.507 --> 52:11.443
This is the way
to get out of here.

52:19.917 --> 52:21.819
Wonder where we are now.

52:21.852 --> 52:23.922
It seems to be safe.

52:23.955 --> 52:25.256
There you are.

52:25.289 --> 52:27.559
TORY:
It's Yuko.

52:29.293 --> 52:32.297
( Pokémon chattering )

52:33.531 --> 52:35.467
( panting )

52:40.004 --> 52:41.673
Munch.

52:44.942 --> 52:46.478
Munch?

52:47.645 --> 52:49.948
Munch. Munch.

52:49.981 --> 52:51.683
Munch.

52:51.716 --> 52:53.818
( wind gusting )

52:53.851 --> 52:55.587
( Rayquaza howls )

52:55.620 --> 52:57.789
( Rayquaza roars )

53:01.592 --> 53:02.961
POLICEWOMAN:
Professor, take a look

53:02.994 --> 53:05.230
at all of these people
shown here.

53:05.263 --> 53:07.332
Their evacuation
hasn't been confirmed

53:07.365 --> 53:09.968
at any
of the passport checkpoints.

53:10.001 --> 53:11.469
I'm afraid that could mean

53:11.502 --> 53:13.004
they're still stuck
in Larousse.

53:13.037 --> 53:14.806
( grunts )

53:19.477 --> 53:21.613
The entire town is enclosed
within a force field.

53:21.646 --> 53:25.250
It's impossible for anyone
to come in or to leave.

53:25.283 --> 53:26.851
All communication
with the outside

53:26.884 --> 53:28.353
is jammed as well.

53:28.386 --> 53:30.321
They've switched
to backup generators,

53:30.354 --> 53:32.457
but all systems
are still down.

53:32.490 --> 53:34.692
Even the Poké Ball
Management System

53:34.725 --> 53:35.893
isn't functioning.

53:35.926 --> 53:37.528
Yeah, it won't work.

53:37.561 --> 53:39.697
How can we call out
our Pokémon?

53:39.730 --> 53:41.032
Guess we can't.

53:41.065 --> 53:44.402
Hey, Tory,
what did you call that thing?

53:44.435 --> 53:46.004
Was it Deoxys?
Hmm-mm.

53:46.037 --> 53:47.372
That's right.

53:47.405 --> 53:49.774
A Pokémon from outer space.

53:49.807 --> 53:51.309
What?

53:51.342 --> 53:53.845
Four years ago,
a meteorite came down

53:53.878 --> 53:55.313
and struck the North Pole.

53:55.346 --> 53:57.282
And located inside of it

53:57.315 --> 53:58.883
was a completely
unknown Pokémon.

53:58.916 --> 54:01.819
 It was Professor Lund
who gave that Pokémon

54:01.852 --> 54:03.354
 the name Deoxys.

54:03.387 --> 54:04.622
( roaring )

54:04.655 --> 54:06.357
 But then almost
immediately,

54:06.390 --> 54:08.026
 Rayquaza appeared
from the ozone

54:08.059 --> 54:09.527
 and attacked Deoxys.

54:11.762 --> 54:14.632
( roars )

54:14.665 --> 54:16.801
 Apparently,
Rayquaza was threatened

54:16.834 --> 54:19.671
 and thought Deoxys
was invading its territory.

54:19.704 --> 54:23.708
 Deoxys vanished deep
into the sea.

54:25.943 --> 54:29.013
BROCK:
I don't get it. How could it be
the same Deoxys?

54:29.046 --> 54:30.782
After getting beaten
by Rayquaza,

54:30.815 --> 54:33.751
Deoxys must have slowly
been regenerating.

54:33.784 --> 54:34.919
Regenerating?

54:34.952 --> 54:36.387
That's right,

54:36.420 --> 54:38.389
it has astounding
regenerative powers.

54:38.422 --> 54:40.391
And that's
what Professor Lund and I

54:40.424 --> 54:41.826
have been studying
all these years.

54:47.598 --> 54:50.535
REBECCA:
It sounds more
like science fiction.

54:50.568 --> 54:52.804
This is something
I'd love to research.

54:52.837 --> 54:55.606
But I wonder if
it could somehow get in

54:55.639 --> 54:57.375
through a crack in the wall.

54:58.109 --> 54:59.577
Knock it off, Max.

54:59.610 --> 55:01.412
Yeah, stop scaring us
right now.

55:01.445 --> 55:02.914
( laughing ):
Just kidding.

55:02.947 --> 55:05.416
There's no way it's coming in
through a crack.

55:05.449 --> 55:07.352
( door opens )
What was that?

55:07.385 --> 55:09.420
Come on, Blaziken.

55:09.453 --> 55:10.655
Blaze. Blaze.

55:10.688 --> 55:13.524
( suspenseful theme playing )

55:13.557 --> 55:15.694
( clanging and rumbling )

55:19.830 --> 55:22.367
Blaze.
Pika.

55:25.069 --> 55:27.004
( both chattering )

55:27.037 --> 55:28.740
Oh!
Pika!

55:34.078 --> 55:35.580
Munch.

55:36.480 --> 55:37.648
Hey, that's the Pokémon

55:37.681 --> 55:39.651
that ate every bite
of our food.

55:40.751 --> 55:42.887
Are you stuck in there,
Munchlax?

55:42.920 --> 55:44.889
Let's see.

55:44.922 --> 55:46.891
( grunting )

55:50.194 --> 55:51.596
Our sandwiches.

55:51.629 --> 55:53.898
Everything
but the peanut butter. Hmm.

55:53.931 --> 55:56.968
And, of course,
that one was mine.

55:59.904 --> 56:01.539
Hold on. Hold on.

56:05.009 --> 56:09.381
Okay, please just don't come
any closer, you two.

56:10.915 --> 56:13.418
Pika. Pikachu.

56:15.085 --> 56:17.121
Munch.
( sighs )

56:17.154 --> 56:19.924
I'm so hungry.
So am I.

56:19.957 --> 56:21.726
Me too.
Mu--

56:21.759 --> 56:22.894
Mu--?

56:22.927 --> 56:24.028
Munchlax.

56:24.061 --> 56:25.563
Really? I can have it?

56:25.596 --> 56:27.966
Munch. Munch. Munch.

56:31.135 --> 56:33.871
ALL: No, thanks.
Munch.

56:33.904 --> 56:36.941
( all gasp and sigh )

56:45.149 --> 56:47.518
BROCK:
We have to find food and water
right away.

56:47.551 --> 56:51.489
Great. And I'll try and find out
where those people were taken.

56:51.522 --> 56:54.091
Yuko, take care
of my sisters, please.

56:54.124 --> 56:56.694
Of course,
but don't you worry about us.

56:56.727 --> 56:58.062
You take care of yourselves.

56:58.095 --> 56:59.530
RAFE:
We will.

56:59.563 --> 57:01.633
ASH:
All right, let's go.

57:05.970 --> 57:09.207
Munchlax.

57:09.240 --> 57:11.742
Munchlax.

57:11.775 --> 57:14.045
( indistinct chattering )

57:14.078 --> 57:16.014
( sighs )

57:17.615 --> 57:19.217
I'm worried, Max.

57:19.250 --> 57:22.153
I really hope
they're all okay.

57:22.186 --> 57:23.554
Yeah, me too.

57:23.587 --> 57:25.556
I wish they'd hurry
and come back.

57:25.589 --> 57:27.625
( speaks indistinctly
)

57:34.031 --> 57:36.634
Still no good.
Nothing's happening.

57:36.667 --> 57:38.970
Yeah. It must be tied
into the town's system.

57:39.003 --> 57:40.705
I can see the food
in there too.

57:40.738 --> 57:43.274
We just need to figure out
a way to break in.

57:43.307 --> 57:45.109
Pika. Pika.
Hmm?            Hmm?

57:45.142 --> 57:48.012
Pikachu!

57:54.051 --> 57:55.186
It worked.

57:55.219 --> 57:57.755
Pikachu, great idea.
Pikachu.

57:58.856 --> 58:01.926
Whoa, gotta catch them all.

58:01.959 --> 58:04.896
Pika.

58:04.929 --> 58:08.132
Pikachu. Pika?

58:08.165 --> 58:10.601
Huh? What is it, Pikachu?

58:10.634 --> 58:11.903
( all gasp )

58:14.572 --> 58:16.007
Look out!
Run!

58:16.040 --> 58:17.509
Pika!

58:21.178 --> 58:23.548
Pika!
Look out!

58:27.151 --> 58:28.286
Plusle. Minun.

58:28.319 --> 58:30.054
( both screaming )

58:31.822 --> 58:33.157
ASH: Put me down!
BROCK: Let go!

58:33.190 --> 58:36.060
( grunts )

58:38.095 --> 58:40.565
Pikachu!

58:40.598 --> 58:42.099
( all grunts )

58:42.132 --> 58:45.036
No!
( whimpers )

58:45.069 --> 58:47.838
( screaming )

58:47.871 --> 58:50.575
Pika.
( gasps )

58:53.077 --> 58:55.713
Here they all come, guys.
Pika.

58:55.746 --> 58:57.815
Come on, Tory,
let's go.

59:03.020 --> 59:05.156
( suspenseful theme playing )

59:18.702 --> 59:20.304
Looks like they're all gone.

59:20.337 --> 59:22.574
That was close.

59:23.707 --> 59:25.776
Oh, Plusle.

59:25.809 --> 59:27.678
It's all my fault.

59:27.711 --> 59:30.047
I should've.

59:30.080 --> 59:32.016
( sighs )

59:35.152 --> 59:36.621
I'm sorry.

59:36.654 --> 59:38.823
Pika. Pika. Pika.

59:38.856 --> 59:40.658
Pikachu.

59:42.359 --> 59:44.061
BROCK:
Ash,

59:44.094 --> 59:46.697
look what I just found.

59:46.730 --> 59:49.934
Precious water.
ASH: All right!

59:57.875 --> 59:59.343
RAFE:
Okay, so that's where

59:59.376 --> 01:00:01.779
they're holding everyone
captive.

01:00:01.812 --> 01:00:04.415
I guess,
but what in the world for?

01:00:04.448 --> 01:00:06.183
ROBOT:
 Release immediately.

01:00:06.216 --> 01:00:08.719
 Release immediately.

01:00:08.752 --> 01:00:11.288
( weakened ):
 Release immediately.

01:00:11.321 --> 01:00:15.026
 Release immediate--

01:00:20.431 --> 01:00:22.867
It let go.

01:00:22.900 --> 01:00:24.636
But why?

01:00:30.774 --> 01:00:33.745
( Rayquaza howls )

01:00:40.350 --> 01:00:42.654
( all snoring )

01:00:51.729 --> 01:00:53.230
Hmm, go back.

01:00:53.263 --> 01:00:55.266
Let me just take
another look at that.

01:00:55.299 --> 01:00:56.768
Sure.

01:01:01.338 --> 01:01:02.873
Surskit. Surskit.

01:01:02.906 --> 01:01:05.910
What is it? What's wrong?

01:01:08.512 --> 01:01:10.815
Pika.

01:01:10.848 --> 01:01:12.216
( object clatters )
Blaze?

01:01:22.960 --> 01:01:25.329
( both scream )
Let's get out of here.

01:01:25.362 --> 01:01:27.965
YOKU:
Yes, there's an underground
laboratory.

01:01:27.998 --> 01:01:30.334
Let's go. Follow me.

01:01:30.367 --> 01:01:32.203
MAX: Munchlax.
Munch?

01:01:32.236 --> 01:01:33.871
Munch. Munch. Munch.

01:01:38.008 --> 01:01:40.478
Try and stay calm.
Now go.

01:01:40.511 --> 01:01:42.814
( dramatic theme playing )

01:02:01.131 --> 01:02:03.834
We should be safe down here
for the time being.

01:02:03.867 --> 01:02:06.204
RAFE: That's good.
BLAZE: Blaze. Blaze.

01:02:08.238 --> 01:02:09.874
Pika.

01:02:13.010 --> 01:02:14.178
ASH:
What's this?

01:02:14.211 --> 01:02:15.946
YOKU:
The lab where we studied Deoxys

01:02:15.979 --> 01:02:17.448
and its regeneration.

01:02:17.481 --> 01:02:20.017
There were actually two
of them before.

01:02:20.050 --> 01:02:21.886
Rayquaza defeated one

01:02:21.919 --> 01:02:24.321
while the other Deoxys
was still dormant

01:02:24.354 --> 01:02:25.990
inside of this meteorite.

01:02:26.023 --> 01:02:27.391
TERESA:
So then you're saying that--

01:02:27.424 --> 01:02:29.393
YOKU:
Yes. That crystal,

01:02:29.426 --> 01:02:31.095
it's a part of Deoxys.

01:02:31.128 --> 01:02:32.530
Part of--

01:02:32.563 --> 01:02:34.999
What do you mean?
Pika.

01:02:38.268 --> 01:02:39.370
( all gasp )

01:02:44.441 --> 01:02:45.943
Pika.

01:02:48.078 --> 01:02:50.447
What?
Hey, Tory, it's your friend.

01:02:50.480 --> 01:02:52.283
Pika.

01:02:52.316 --> 01:02:55.419
Wait a second.
Then Tory's friend is--

01:02:55.452 --> 01:02:57.421
Right. It's Deoxys.

01:02:57.454 --> 01:02:58.923
( all gasp )

01:03:14.404 --> 01:03:15.973
Huh?

01:03:16.006 --> 01:03:18.810
That's it.
It all makes sense.

01:03:20.978 --> 01:03:23.881
This is Tory's friend's
light pattern.

01:03:25.215 --> 01:03:27.518
And this is the pattern
of the aurora

01:03:27.551 --> 01:03:29.920
that covered Larousse.

01:03:29.953 --> 01:03:31.322
It's the same.

01:03:31.355 --> 01:03:33.924
Yeah, I think it might be
how they communicate.

01:03:33.957 --> 01:03:37.561
Oh, I see.
So can you tell what it says?

01:03:37.594 --> 01:03:40.965
TERESA:
Well, let's start
with the green pattern.

01:03:42.332 --> 01:03:45.069
This one means friend.

01:03:45.102 --> 01:03:47.304
And this one seems
to be asking,

01:03:47.337 --> 01:03:49.240
"Where are you?"

01:03:49.273 --> 01:03:51.342
So it's just looking
for its friend?

01:03:51.375 --> 01:03:52.209
Pika.

01:03:52.243 --> 01:03:54.478
YOKU:
Of course. Deoxys carried off

01:03:54.511 --> 01:03:57.615
all those people and Pokémon
because they were interfering

01:03:57.648 --> 01:03:59.550
while it searched
for its friend.

01:03:59.583 --> 01:04:01.352
What?
Deoxys sees certain types

01:04:01.385 --> 01:04:02.486
of electrical fields.

01:04:02.519 --> 01:04:04.588
But it's not only
electrical devices

01:04:04.621 --> 01:04:07.358
that give off those fields,
so do people and Pokémon,

01:04:07.391 --> 01:04:11.262
and they were blocking
its vision.

01:04:11.295 --> 01:04:13.898
That's why it's moving them
out of the way,

01:04:13.931 --> 01:04:15.333
to find it.

01:04:18.168 --> 01:04:21.138
( dramatic theme playing )

01:04:42.059 --> 01:04:44.362
( gasps and sighs )

01:04:52.703 --> 01:04:58.542
Please, Yuko, you've got
to help this Deoxys regenerate.

01:04:58.575 --> 01:05:00.277
It's so sad.

01:05:00.310 --> 01:05:02.346
It's been alone
all of this time.

01:05:02.379 --> 01:05:06.984
You're right. Once Deoxys finds
its friend, it'll go back home.

01:05:07.017 --> 01:05:08.319
Pikachu.
But the problem is,

01:05:08.352 --> 01:05:10.220
the emergency power
we're running on now

01:05:10.253 --> 01:05:13.157
isn't nearly enough necessary
to operate this device.

01:05:13.190 --> 01:05:16.160
If it's electricity you want,
then I'm your guy.

01:05:16.193 --> 01:05:18.228
I can get
the wind generators going.

01:05:18.261 --> 01:05:19.596
Can we help?
Can we help?

01:05:19.629 --> 01:05:21.265
Yes, we'll need everyone's help

01:05:21.298 --> 01:05:23.033
to save those people
and Pokémon.

01:05:23.066 --> 01:05:24.468
Let's start working
on a plan,

01:05:24.501 --> 01:05:26.670
and then we'll go out
to where they're being held.

01:05:26.703 --> 01:05:28.539
I'll zero in on it.

01:05:29.639 --> 01:05:31.041
That's where they all are.

01:05:31.074 --> 01:05:33.110
ASH:
Great. Let's go get them, guys.

01:05:33.143 --> 01:05:34.378
ALL:
All right!

01:05:34.411 --> 01:05:38.549
( suspenseful theme playing )

01:05:42.519 --> 01:05:44.488
( all chattering )

01:05:53.530 --> 01:05:55.532
( panting )

01:05:55.565 --> 01:05:59.403
I'll never take an escalator
for granted again.

01:06:14.117 --> 01:06:16.087
( grunts )

01:06:18.555 --> 01:06:22.526
Deoxys, we're not your enemies.
We're your friends.

01:06:25.062 --> 01:06:26.330
If you'll just trust us,

01:06:26.363 --> 01:06:28.599
we can help you
find your friend. I promise.

01:06:33.103 --> 01:06:35.439
Blaziken, use Flamethrower now.

01:06:40.343 --> 01:06:44.048
Pikachu, Thunderbolt him.
Pikachu!

01:06:47.317 --> 01:06:51.088
Metagross, use Reflector.

01:06:51.121 --> 01:06:52.389
Meta!

01:06:52.422 --> 01:06:54.191
TERESA:
Quick, now's our chance.

01:06:54.224 --> 01:06:56.027
TORY:
This way.

01:06:59.162 --> 01:07:01.331
Now, Overheat.

01:07:01.364 --> 01:07:02.466
Blaze!

01:07:04.868 --> 01:07:06.770
You okay?

01:07:06.803 --> 01:07:09.473
We're fine, Ash.
Just go on.

01:07:09.506 --> 01:07:11.675
Rafe can handle it.

01:07:11.708 --> 01:07:15.145
Just don't let anything happen
to my sisters, Ash.

01:07:15.178 --> 01:07:18.082
You can count on that.

01:07:19.449 --> 01:07:22.420
Blaziken, Overheat!
Blaze.

01:07:27.791 --> 01:07:30.327
( roars )

01:07:46.910 --> 01:07:49.880
Rayquaza has broken through.

01:07:49.913 --> 01:07:51.382
What have I done?

01:07:59.489 --> 01:08:02.392
Blaze....

01:08:02.425 --> 01:08:04.528
Relax, Blaziken.
Blaze.

01:08:12.469 --> 01:08:14.438
( roars )

01:08:39.663 --> 01:08:41.599
( all chattering )

01:08:42.699 --> 01:08:44.668
( roars )

01:08:45.869 --> 01:08:47.638
Rayquaza.
Now what's that?

01:08:47.671 --> 01:08:49.673
( roaring )

01:09:01.918 --> 01:09:05.389
All right, now let's do it
just like we planned. Okay guys?

01:09:05.422 --> 01:09:06.523
BROCK:
Got you.

01:09:06.556 --> 01:09:08.559
TERESA:
We're with you, Ash.

01:09:10.994 --> 01:09:12.930
Munch. Munch. Munch.

01:09:12.963 --> 01:09:14.665
Munchlax.

01:09:14.698 --> 01:09:17.201
Come on, there's no time for you
to go back for it.

01:09:17.234 --> 01:09:19.203
Oh, Munchlax!

01:09:26.743 --> 01:09:28.912
You ready?
Just about.

01:09:28.945 --> 01:09:30.547
All we need
is the electricity.

01:09:30.580 --> 01:09:33.817
But if we had that,
we wouldn't need to fix it.

01:09:33.850 --> 01:09:36.353
What are they doing over there?

01:09:36.386 --> 01:09:39.323
I'm hoping he pulls a sandwich
out of that box.

01:09:39.356 --> 01:09:42.292
From your lips,
to my stomach.

01:09:42.325 --> 01:09:43.694
ASH:
You guys,

01:09:43.727 --> 01:09:45.729
we've come to help you.

01:09:45.762 --> 01:09:47.965
Hey, Ash, we're up here.

01:09:47.998 --> 01:09:50.000
You got Pikachu
and Plusle, right?

01:09:50.033 --> 01:09:52.436
Yeah. We're all set.

01:09:52.469 --> 01:09:53.604
Pika.

01:09:54.738 --> 01:09:56.707
( Rayquaza roars )

01:10:00.910 --> 01:10:03.714
( suspenseful theme playing )

01:10:20.664 --> 01:10:22.633
( roars )

01:10:34.644 --> 01:10:36.614
( growls )

01:10:40.650 --> 01:10:42.619
ASH: Pikachu.
TORY: Plusle.

01:10:42.652 --> 01:10:44.388
BOTH:
Thunderbolt, now.

01:10:48.058 --> 01:10:49.893
SID:
There's your electricity.

01:10:49.926 --> 01:10:52.029
( Pikachu screams )

01:10:52.062 --> 01:10:53.631
That's good. Stop.

01:10:54.731 --> 01:10:57.268
All right.
We're recharged.

01:10:59.936 --> 01:11:01.371
Yeah!

01:11:01.404 --> 01:11:03.407
All right.

01:11:05.942 --> 01:11:08.378
( grunting ):
Ouch.

01:11:08.411 --> 01:11:10.314
( both chattering )

01:11:13.683 --> 01:11:15.319
( both scream )

01:11:22.092 --> 01:11:24.428
You were great, Tory.

01:11:25.162 --> 01:11:27.698
( heroic theme playing )

01:11:33.002 --> 01:11:34.471
( laughs )

01:11:38.842 --> 01:11:40.844
( roars )

01:11:52.756 --> 01:11:54.725
( all panting )

01:11:57.694 --> 01:11:59.730
( roars )

01:12:06.403 --> 01:12:07.905
Let's go.
Yeah.

01:12:11.141 --> 01:12:13.877
( grunts )

01:12:13.910 --> 01:12:15.879
That should do it.

01:12:15.912 --> 01:12:18.382
Coming down!

01:12:18.415 --> 01:12:19.716
( grunts )

01:12:19.749 --> 01:12:21.685
( groans )

01:12:28.892 --> 01:12:31.895
SID:
Hey, May, I'm coming for you.

01:12:31.928 --> 01:12:33.397
Was that Sid?

01:12:33.430 --> 01:12:35.866
BOTH:
Uh, and Rafe!

01:12:35.899 --> 01:12:38.101
May!

01:12:38.134 --> 01:12:39.970
( grunts )

01:12:40.003 --> 01:12:41.671
Gross.

01:12:41.704 --> 01:12:42.840
Metagross.

01:12:44.174 --> 01:12:45.876
Audrey, Kathryn,
you okay?

01:12:45.909 --> 01:12:47.611
KATHRYN: Uh-huh.
AUDREY: We're fine.

01:12:47.644 --> 01:12:49.146
Where's Ash and the others?

01:12:49.179 --> 01:12:50.814
They went back
to the laboratory.

01:12:50.847 --> 01:12:53.917
Okay, are you ready
to get started on this?

01:12:53.950 --> 01:12:55.919
( switches clicking )

01:13:06.796 --> 01:13:08.665
Perfect, the power's
back on.

01:13:08.698 --> 01:13:10.434
Yeah, those guys
pulled it off.

01:13:10.467 --> 01:13:11.735
Mm-hmm.

01:13:19.008 --> 01:13:20.978
( all grunting )

01:13:35.658 --> 01:13:37.828
( all chattering )

01:13:43.032 --> 01:13:45.235
Blaziken. Blaziken.

01:13:45.268 --> 01:13:48.539
Metagross.

01:14:01.284 --> 01:14:03.520
( all groaning )

01:14:03.553 --> 01:14:05.655
My cramp's
getting a cramp.

01:14:05.688 --> 01:14:07.691
We're always spinning
our wheels

01:14:07.724 --> 01:14:10.126
but this is ridiculous.

01:14:10.159 --> 01:14:11.895
Just pedal!

01:14:23.239 --> 01:14:26.243
I'm set. Are you both ready
to use the laser?

01:14:26.276 --> 01:14:29.613
Yes. I think
you should turn it on, Tory.

01:14:29.646 --> 01:14:31.848
It is your friend after all,

01:14:31.881 --> 01:14:33.750
so you should do it.

01:14:38.154 --> 01:14:39.623
Hmm.

01:14:46.029 --> 01:14:47.531
Here goes.

01:14:50.667 --> 01:14:53.704
( dramatic theme playing )

01:15:07.216 --> 01:15:09.786
Pika.

01:15:17.594 --> 01:15:19.663
TORY:
Still no good.

01:15:23.066 --> 01:15:24.334
Oh, no,

01:15:24.367 --> 01:15:26.336
we're still 20 percent short
on energy.

01:15:26.369 --> 01:15:28.305
Wow, we're so close.

01:15:28.338 --> 01:15:29.973
Okay, Pikachu,

01:15:30.006 --> 01:15:32.175
Plusle, Minun,
you know what to do.

01:15:32.208 --> 01:15:33.910
Pika.

01:15:33.943 --> 01:15:37.748
Pikachu!
( both shouting )

01:15:43.086 --> 01:15:45.822
( upbeat theme playing )

01:15:58.001 --> 01:16:00.670
Great idea,
we got just what we need.

01:16:00.703 --> 01:16:02.939
It works.
All right.

01:16:02.972 --> 01:16:05.142
( all shouting )

01:16:16.152 --> 01:16:19.089
( glass shattering )

01:16:19.122 --> 01:16:20.991
( all gasp )

01:16:34.203 --> 01:16:36.206
( dramatic theme playing )

01:16:41.144 --> 01:16:43.380
We did it!

01:16:43.413 --> 01:16:46.717
Oh, Deoxys,
it's really you.

01:16:52.288 --> 01:16:54.224
( chuckles )

01:17:00.163 --> 01:17:01.765
Pika!

01:17:17.947 --> 01:17:20.984
Deoxys, do you wanna go
find your friend now?

01:17:29.292 --> 01:17:31.662
( both laugh )
Pika.

01:17:33.963 --> 01:17:35.065
Pika.

01:17:41.504 --> 01:17:43.073
Pika!

01:17:48.778 --> 01:17:50.681
ASH & TORY:
Whoa!

01:17:57.253 --> 01:17:59.222
( roars )

01:18:13.169 --> 01:18:15.172
( all gasping )

01:18:33.523 --> 01:18:36.960
The force field's gone.
Just like that?

01:18:43.332 --> 01:18:44.835
( roars )

01:18:56.946 --> 01:18:58.949
( heroic theme playing )

01:19:00.883 --> 01:19:02.986
( roaring )

01:19:29.312 --> 01:19:31.314
( whimpers )
Pika.

01:19:44.627 --> 01:19:47.163
( Rayquaza roars )

01:19:47.196 --> 01:19:49.065
( both gasp )
Pika.

01:20:18.928 --> 01:20:23.033
( mellow theme playing )

01:20:52.662 --> 01:20:54.397
( both gasp )
Pika.

01:21:03.072 --> 01:21:04.875
( both chattering )

01:21:24.527 --> 01:21:27.097
( laughing ):
Pika.

01:21:39.008 --> 01:21:40.277
( both gasp )
Pika!

01:21:43.212 --> 01:21:45.348
( suspenseful theme playing )

01:21:58.728 --> 01:22:00.063
Hey, knock it off!

01:22:00.096 --> 01:22:02.198
Stop, Rayquaza.
Pika.

01:22:04.734 --> 01:22:06.202
( roaring )

01:22:31.360 --> 01:22:33.296
( roars )

01:22:37.466 --> 01:22:40.737
 Warning! Warning!
Warning!

01:22:40.770 --> 01:22:44.407
 Danger! Danger! Danger!

01:22:46.409 --> 01:22:49.412
 Evacuate! Evacuate!

01:22:49.445 --> 01:22:50.680
What happened?

01:22:50.713 --> 01:22:53.483
Security somehow started up.

01:23:11.500 --> 01:23:14.170
 Warning! Evacuate!

01:23:14.203 --> 01:23:17.106
 Warning! Evacuate!

01:23:17.139 --> 01:23:18.341
 Warning!

01:23:18.374 --> 01:23:21.110
( weakening ):
 Evacuate.

01:23:21.143 --> 01:23:25.081
 Warning. E-vac-u-ate.

01:23:44.433 --> 01:23:47.103
Somehow security
has gone on overdrive.

01:23:47.136 --> 01:23:48.671
It won't shut down.

01:23:48.704 --> 01:23:49.806
Yuko.

01:23:49.839 --> 01:23:51.441
Professor Lund.

01:23:51.474 --> 01:23:53.309
( roaring )

01:24:26.275 --> 01:24:28.478
Everything's
totally out of control.

01:24:28.511 --> 01:24:29.612
Ash, I'm scared.

01:24:37.620 --> 01:24:39.889
Rayquaza. Deoxys.

01:24:39.922 --> 01:24:41.557
Pika!

01:24:41.590 --> 01:24:43.159
Whoa!

01:24:44.293 --> 01:24:47.130
Plusle. Minun.
Pikachu.

01:24:47.163 --> 01:24:48.297
Pika.

01:24:48.330 --> 01:24:50.133
They almost hit us that time.

01:24:50.166 --> 01:24:51.734
Let's try and get back
to Yuko.

01:24:51.767 --> 01:24:54.403
 Tory, can you hear me? Tory?

01:24:54.436 --> 01:24:55.337
Daddy.

01:24:55.371 --> 01:24:57.707
 You must listen
to me very carefully.

01:24:57.740 --> 01:25:01.244
 As you can see, all the block
robots are malfunctioning.

01:25:01.277 --> 01:25:02.478
The chief robot,

01:25:02.511 --> 01:25:04.247
which controls
all other block robots,

01:25:04.280 --> 01:25:05.648
should be near you.

01:25:05.681 --> 01:25:09.218
We no longer have power
over that robot from the booth.

01:25:09.251 --> 01:25:12.255
Understand?
So here's what you have to do.

01:25:12.288 --> 01:25:14.323
And I need for you to be brave.

01:25:14.356 --> 01:25:16.759
 Tory, do you have
your passport?

01:25:16.792 --> 01:25:19.862
 You must present your passport
to the chief robot.

01:25:19.895 --> 01:25:21.597
 Then everything should unlock

01:25:21.630 --> 01:25:24.233
 but only
for a very brief moment.

01:25:24.266 --> 01:25:25.501
 That should allow us

01:25:25.534 --> 01:25:27.503
 just enough time
to regain control.

01:25:27.536 --> 01:25:30.373
 And shut down
the security system.

01:25:30.406 --> 01:25:32.575
 Block robots are surrounding
the battle tower

01:25:32.608 --> 01:25:35.311
 making any approach by us
impossible.

01:25:35.344 --> 01:25:37.847
 Son, the fate of our town
is in your hands.

01:25:37.880 --> 01:25:40.283
 I know we can count on you--

01:25:46.555 --> 01:25:49.692
ROBOT:
 Warning! Evacuate!

01:25:49.725 --> 01:25:50.893
 Warning!

01:25:50.926 --> 01:25:53.896
( weakening ):
 Eva--

01:25:53.929 --> 01:25:55.565
( suspenseful theme playing )

01:26:02.805 --> 01:26:04.373
Don't you worry, sir.

01:26:04.406 --> 01:26:06.209
Pikachu and I
are gonna help Tory

01:26:06.242 --> 01:26:07.777
save this town together.

01:26:07.810 --> 01:26:09.279
Pika.

01:26:10.546 --> 01:26:12.448
ASH:
We've gotta get to that tower.

01:26:15.284 --> 01:26:18.388
Look at that.
Quick, let's go.

01:26:28.030 --> 01:26:29.899
Okay. Just a little more.

01:26:29.932 --> 01:26:31.434
ALL:
Whoa!

01:26:31.467 --> 01:26:33.970
Munch, Munch, Munch.

01:26:34.003 --> 01:26:36.472
Munchlax?
( all scream )

01:26:46.715 --> 01:26:48.317
Snorlax.

01:26:48.350 --> 01:26:51.354
A Snorlax. That's it.

01:26:53.689 --> 01:26:55.291
Sorry.

01:27:00.729 --> 01:27:01.864
Pika.

01:27:01.897 --> 01:27:03.366
TORY:
Hey, Ash.

01:27:04.933 --> 01:27:07.470
Tory, don't worry.
I'm okay.

01:27:07.503 --> 01:27:09.739
I'll take care of this.

01:27:13.709 --> 01:27:15.544
Pika.

01:27:15.577 --> 01:27:16.679
Pikachu.

01:27:20.582 --> 01:27:21.450
Pika!

01:27:21.483 --> 01:27:25.054
Oh, wow, cool.
I'm right behind you.

01:27:25.087 --> 01:27:27.390
( grunting )

01:27:35.864 --> 01:27:38.434
Pika! Pika!

01:27:47.676 --> 01:27:48.778
No!

01:27:51.080 --> 01:27:53.382
Oh, no.
Pikachu.

01:27:53.415 --> 01:27:54.984
TORY:
Ash!

01:27:55.017 --> 01:27:57.653
Use my passport!
Throw it.

01:27:57.686 --> 01:27:58.821
( grunts )

01:28:05.394 --> 01:28:06.663
Pika.

01:28:09.365 --> 01:28:11.667
Pika.

01:28:11.700 --> 01:28:12.835
Pikachu!

01:28:12.868 --> 01:28:17.373
Pika, Pika. Pikachu.

01:28:35.991 --> 01:28:38.861
This better work.

01:28:40.729 --> 01:28:43.366
COMPUTER:
 Passport has been verified.

01:28:43.399 --> 01:28:45.835
 Disengaging all locks.

01:28:45.868 --> 01:28:46.969
I'm almost there.

01:28:47.002 --> 01:28:48.905
Disengage.

01:28:52.775 --> 01:28:53.876
( chimes )

01:29:18.167 --> 01:29:20.503
It worked, guys.

01:29:25.507 --> 01:29:27.643
( grunts )

01:29:29.778 --> 01:29:31.647
Oh, no, Tory.

01:29:37.052 --> 01:29:39.455
( heroic theme playing )

01:29:40.989 --> 01:29:42.124
Deoxys.

01:29:42.157 --> 01:29:43.626
( laughs )

01:29:47.729 --> 01:29:48.831
Pika.

01:29:50.732 --> 01:29:51.934
Pikachu.

01:29:58.674 --> 01:29:59.776
Pika.

01:30:02.845 --> 01:30:04.814
( chuckles )

01:30:06.982 --> 01:30:09.585
Pika! Pika!

01:30:11.220 --> 01:30:13.556
( chuckling )

01:30:17.092 --> 01:30:19.662
Pika. Pika.
( laughs )

01:30:19.695 --> 01:30:21.731
Pika!

01:30:31.240 --> 01:30:33.543
( roars )

01:30:41.049 --> 01:30:44.554
SNORLAX:
Snorlax.

01:30:47.990 --> 01:30:49.959
( all chuckling )

01:30:59.234 --> 01:31:01.070
Tory.
Daddy.

01:31:01.103 --> 01:31:03.239
( Tory laughs )

01:31:03.272 --> 01:31:05.608
Tory.
Hi, Dad.

01:31:05.641 --> 01:31:08.043
I'm so happy
you're safe.

01:31:08.076 --> 01:31:12.615
But I'm only okay
because of my friends.

01:31:25.627 --> 01:31:27.897
TORY:
Come on, guys. That tickles.

01:31:41.310 --> 01:31:42.878
PIKACHU:
Pika.

01:31:42.911 --> 01:31:45.081
( majestic theme playing )

01:31:53.055 --> 01:31:55.925
Goodbye. I'll miss you.

01:32:00.796 --> 01:32:03.065
I wonder where
they're going.

01:32:03.098 --> 01:32:04.767
Yeah.

01:32:04.800 --> 01:32:08.170
But now, wherever they go,
they'll always have each other.

01:32:08.203 --> 01:32:10.072
Pikachu.

01:32:23.051 --> 01:32:24.152
Hey, Pikachu?

01:32:24.186 --> 01:32:27.590
I'm glad that you and I
will always have each other.

01:32:27.623 --> 01:32:30.759
Pika. Pikachu.

01:32:30.792 --> 01:32:32.662
( Bree Sharp's
"This Side of Paradise" plays )

01:32:35.297 --> 01:32:37.933
I must have lost
20 pounds so far.

01:32:37.966 --> 01:32:39.702
And you already lost
your mind.

01:32:39.735 --> 01:32:41.604
And I'm losing
my patience,

01:32:41.637 --> 01:32:44.139
so just shut up
and keep pedaling!

01:32:44.172 --> 01:32:45.908
 ♪ La, la, la, la, la ♪

01:32:45.941 --> 01:32:50.680
 ♪ La, la, la, la, la
La, la, la, la, la ♪

01:32:52.848 --> 01:32:54.850
 ♪ There's a place I know ♪

01:32:54.883 --> 01:32:56.852
 ♪ It's always jumping ♪

01:32:56.885 --> 01:33:00.990
 ♪ I'm thinking we should go
And leave our worries ♪

01:33:01.023 --> 01:33:03.225
 ♪ You've got a friend in me ♪

01:33:03.258 --> 01:33:05.194
 ♪ And I'll tell you something ♪

01:33:05.227 --> 01:33:09.331
 ♪ This time
Could be extraordinary ♪

01:33:09.364 --> 01:33:13.836
 ♪ When shadows fall
You're feeling small ♪

